Synergy's benchmark/src/synergy_bench/trial.py adapts the separate-verifier
lifecycle from datacurve-pier 0.3.1 (https://pypi.org/project/datacurve-pier/0.3.1/).
Modifications separate cleanup from verifier deadlines, preserve committed
rewards, bound cleanup, and disable automatic environment/verifier timeout retries.
Preparation uses queue-aware deadlines; image cache-key locks replace the
upstream task-name build lock so independent variants can prepare concurrently. The outer
agent deadline preserves Pier's AgentTimeoutError so timed-out agents still
reach native artifact collection and verification.
The dependency version is pinned in benchmark/pyproject.toml and uv.lock.

Synergy's benchmark/src/synergy_bench/agent.py follows the same version's
InstalledAgent._exec agent_process_env integration so isolated task networks
retain Pier-managed inference egress for the agent process.

Synergy's benchmark/src/synergy_bench/environment.py extends the pinned Pier
Docker environment with immutable image receipts, scoped image ownership,
process-tree cancellation and inference-proxy address handling. Native task
Dockerfiles, resource limits, verifier recipes and task network policy remain
owned by Pier and the locked task sources. oracle.py invokes Pier's native
OracleAgent in separate disposable audits.
